<Concept title="HUmar saber Coliseum prototype" section="States">
<p>Issue #790: a scoped experiment in methodical combat. PSZ idle and attacks combine with PSO locomotion, readiness and reactions; the rules below are provisional remake choices for owner playtesting, not verified PSO mechanics. This contract overrides ordinary player timing only in the explicitly enabled HUmar/saber Coliseum fixture.</p>
<p>Broader rollout is planned separately: <a href={siteUrl('/states/weapon-animation-mappings/')}>mapping matrix</a>, <a href={siteUrl('/states/weapon-state-transitions/')}>UML transitions</a>, and <a href={siteUrl('/states/weapon-adaptation-plan/')}>adaptation/test plans</a>.</p>
<ul>
<li>The prototype MUST use the current PSZ HUmar VRM and the complete mapped PSO saber set, source clips 097–111. Clips 112–113 belong to sword. Native PSZ pmsa_wait and pmsa_atk1–3 MUST supply relaxed idle and actual attacks. PSO attack and utility clips remain available for inspection even when the encounter does not invoke them.</li>
<li>Caution MUST engage from the displayed living-enemy cursor during approach/lateral movement, never from proximity alone. Retreat or loss of that cursor MUST retain caution for 500 ms of continuous movement before transitioning directly to run. Reacquisition MUST cancel the countdown; stopping or entering combat MUST reset elapsed retreat time. Without prior cursor engagement, ordinary walk-to-run progression uses general pmsa_walk and PSO saber run. Standing MUST remain PSZ relaxed idle regardless of proximity. Fixed player/enemy levels MUST make repeated encounters comparable.</li>
<li>An idle, walking or finisher-ready Hunter facing an incoming melee attacker within a 60-degree half-angle MAY automatically guard. Attack preparation, active swings, failed-combo recovery, stopped-combo attack cooldown, running, rolling, frozen, damage-recovering, defeated or menu-blocked players MUST NOT start a guard. Guard MUST absorb one physical hit, play the block clip and commit the player until its end. This is deterministic experimental defense, not a stat-based PSO evasion formula.</li>
<li>Guard MUST NOT cancel an attack or cure status effects. Status ticks, ranged attacks and rear hits MUST retain ordinary damage handling. A successful guard MUST NOT award damage-based Photon Blast charge.</li>
<li>Native PSZ saber swings MUST retain native motion speed plus held recovery of 0.14/0.16/0.22 seconds and initially use provisional contact fractions of the motion duration (0.40, 0.40, 0.45), with one contact event per step. Chain input MUST use the prototype window 0.55–0.95, preserve single-slot queuing and commitment, and have no timing damage bonus. These values MUST be visually checked and tuned with owner feedback.</li>
<li>Connected fixture physical hits MUST bypass accuracy-roll misses while preserving geometry, defense and immunity checks. Campaign hit chances MUST remain unchanged.</li>
<li>Normal and strong chains MUST use identical timing, without an added strong-only delay. Strong windup MUST play SE_PL_BIGCHARGE and clear its visual on contact or interruption. Primary enemy cursor acquisition or change MUST play SE_PL_LOCKCURSOR once; unchanged and lost cursors MUST be silent.</li>
<li>Chain timing MUST appear as a shrinking circle on attack palette icons, using the actual shared acceptance window. Ground rings MUST be hidden. Strong windup MUST use small weapon particles. Actual HP loss MUST trigger a subtle contact spark and impact sound; strong hits MAY extend an accepted generic flinch to 0.45 seconds without bypassing immunity.</li>
<li>Both first-attack types MUST share 250 ms of vulnerable weapon-ready preparation. Completed three-step combos MUST earn 350 ms of frontal-guard ready recovery; early or late mistimed input MUST cause 250 ms of stationary exposed recovery after the swing. Deliberately withholding input MUST release movement at swing completion while blocking attacks and guard for 300 ms. Failed and completed recovery forbid attack/dodge cancellation, and damage MUST clear pending phases.</li>
<li>The experiment MUST NOT change campaign, other weapons/classes, EXP, status semantics or global enemy resources. Existing enemy behavior is the baseline; adjust only demonstrated obstacles to this test.</li>
</ul>
<p>Verification requires deterministic guard boundaries and live real-rig checks of all 15 clips, locomotion, attack contact, guard, interruption and recovery. Owner review determines whether the exchange feels fair; passing checks does not raise the Combat or Character grades. Status redesign remains separate in #789.</p>
</Concept>
